WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV v3.0 — rce (180s) Narrator Alice

1
00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.106
First, you write a program once as one clear blueprint,

2
00:00:04.106 --> 00:00:08.056
and the computer generates matching code across languages.

3
00:00:08.616 --> 00:00:13.372
Second, every possible input must have a declared outcome up front,

4
00:00:13.372 --> 00:00:16.708
preventing hidden crashes before anything runs.

5
00:00:17.268 --> 00:00:21.996
Third, every repair that passes the checker is saved and reused,

6
00:00:21.996 --> 00:00:24.581
so you never pay twice for one fix.

7
00:00:25.141 --> 00:00:30.042
Ask a large language model to write code from scratch on every ticket and you

8
00:00:30.042 --> 00:00:36.025
pay full energy to sample a fresh statistical guess each time—even though empirical studies of

9
00:00:36.025 --> 00:00:42.899
public repositories show roughly seventy percent of files are close clones of work already solved elsewhere.

10
00:00:43.459 --> 00:00:51.589
Human requests carry wide ambiguity, yet every processor ultimately executes simple loads, stores, arithmetic,

11
00:00:51.589 --> 00:00:59.646
and jumps. Translating intent across hundreds of surface languages injects silent mismatches at the seams—for

12
00:00:59.646 --> 00:01:06.150
instance, negative three modulo two equals positive one in Python yet negative one in C.

13
00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:15.239
The Reality Code Engine replaces that leaky translation funnel with four steps. First, author intent once as

14
00:01:15.239 --> 00:01:23.610
a lossless state machine called a Form, carrying states, events, and an append-only step log. Second, pass

15
00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:34.587
grammar, type, ownership, and mutation checks. Third, emit byte-matching Rust, Python, JavaScript, and Scala. Fourth, store accepted fixes.

16
00:01:35.147 --> 00:01:42.203
By construction, every input must either step cleanly to a declared state or record an explicit

17
00:01:42.203 --> 00:01:50.669
kept step—eliminating undefined crashes. When solving or repairing tasks, mechanisms run in strict order of energy

18
00:01:50.669 --> 00:01:59.210
cost: microsecond lookup first, guarded rewrite rules second, constraint search third, and neural models only last.

19
00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:07.991
Our three-dimensional polyhedron illustrates one checked state-machine core anchored by a hash-chained event log. Rather than

20
00:02:07.991 --> 00:02:15.093
maintaining four separate codebases that drift from their comments and from one another over years of edits,

21
00:02:15.093 --> 00:02:22.919
every target runtime is a verified mathematical projection of one master blueprint that replays identical event traces.

22
00:02:23.479 --> 00:02:33.734
At public commit one-seven-six-two-f-b-four-b, the Lean 4 audit verifies five thousand five hundred thirty-seven theorem constants across sixty-four

23
00:02:33.734 --> 00:02:43.573
modules with zero unproven placeholders. Two thousand two hundred twenty-one conformance checks and eight hundred thirty-seven Rust unit tests

24
00:02:43.573 --> 00:02:52.996
pass with zero failures, costing forty-nine millijoules per check and fifteen point four joules across all sixty-two example blueprints.

25
00:02:53.556 --> 00:03:02.596
Every open boundary is stated plainly: twelve newer draft-zero-point-nine theorems remain unproved, no production optimizing compiler

26
00:03:02.596 --> 00:03:09.801
ships yet, outside stochastic repairs reached two point five percent above their two percent promotion cap

27
00:03:09.801 --> 00:03:16.734
and remained in observation mode, and all energy figures come from chip counters without a wall meter.
